Herald OS runs on Hermes Agent (https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent),
Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research, released under the MIT License. It uses
Hermes Agent without modifying it, and includes the following material from it:

- apps/desktop/src/assets/brand/hermes-avatar.jpg, the Hermes agent avatar
  (apps/desktop/public/nous-girl.jpg upstream).
- The TypeScript gateway client and generated wire contract
  (apps/shared/src upstream). They are downloaded at build time into
  upstream/hermes-agent/ (pinned by upstream/UPSTREAM.lock), re-exported by
  packages/hermes-client and compiled into the Herald OS shell.

The Hermes Agent runtime itself is not distributed with Herald OS; users
install it separately.

Herald OS is an independent project. It is not an official Hermes Agent or
Nous Research product, and it is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed
by Nous Research.

Third-party npm and Python packages keep their own licenses. A packaged build
includes Electron (MIT, https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/LICENSE)
and Chromium, whose component licenses are listed in LICENSES.chromium.html in
every Electron release. It also includes ONNX Runtime Web (MIT,
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime), which runs Herald Canvas's on-device
models, and ag-psd (MIT, https://github.com/Agamnentzar/ag-psd), which reads and
writes Photoshop documents, with its dependencies pako (MIT and Zlib,
https://github.com/nodeca/pako) and base64-js (MIT,
https://github.com/beatgammit/base64-js). The models themselves are not
distributed with Herald OS: Herald Canvas downloads each from where its
publisher put it, only after the person allows it, and each keeps its own
license (listed in apps/desktop/shared/canvas/models.ts).

Herald Sheets is built on Univer (https://github.com/dream-num/univer),
Copyright 2023-present DreamNum Co., Ltd., released under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. Herald OS uses Univer's open-source packages without modifying
them. They are compiled into the renderer, and a packaged build carries their
license in licenses/univer-LICENSE.txt.

Herald Docs, and the text in Herald Slides, are edited with TipTap (MIT,
https://github.com/ueberdosis/tiptap) and ProseMirror (MIT,
https://prosemirror.net). Herald Office reads and writes Office files with
ExcelJS (MIT, https://github.com/exceljs/exceljs), docx (MIT,
https://github.com/dolanmiu/docx), PptxGenJS (MIT,
https://github.com/gitbrent/PptxGenJS) and JSZip (used under its MIT license,
https://github.com/Stuk/jszip), which also brings in pako.

Herald Sheets draws its charts with Apache ECharts (https://echarts.apache.org),
Copyright 2017-2026 The Apache Software Foundation, released under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. This product includes software developed at The Apache
Software Foundation (https://www.apache.org/). ECharts brings in ZRender
(BSD-3-Clause, https://github.com/ecomfe/zrender), Copyright (c) 2017, Baidu
Inc., and tslib (0BSD, https://github.com/microsoft/tslib). They are compiled
into the renderer without changes.
